      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would it make sense to split out a separate `ai-review-agent-provider-api` target here, similar to how `replication` exposes exposes its shared API in Gerrit core as `replication-api`?\n\nThat would let agent-specific plugins depend only on the provider API, instead of depending on the full `ai-review-agent-provider` plugin implementation.\n\nSomething along these lines:\n\n```python id\u003d\"2rj3v7\"\ngerrit_plugin(\n    name \u003d \"ai-review-agent-provider-api\",\n    srcs \u003d glob([\"src/main/java/com/gerritforge/gerrit/plugins/ai/provider/api/*.java\"]),\n    dir_name \u003d \"ai-review-agent-provider\",\n    manifest_entries \u003d [\n        \"Gerrit-PluginName: ai-review-agent-provider-api\",\n        \"Implementation-Title: AI Review Agent shared provider API\",\n        \"Implementation-URL: https://github.com/GerritForge/ai-review-agent-provider\",\n        \"Gerrit-ApiModule: com.gerritforge.gerrit.plugins.ai.provider.api.AiReviewProviderApiModule\",\n    ],\n)\n```\n\nThen the agent-specific plugins could depend only on that API target, for example:\n\n```diff id\u003d\"g0vwt4\"\ndiff --git a/BUILD b/BUILD\nindex 52137b0..f4dcfd3 100644\n--- a/BUILD\n+++ b/BUILD\n@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@ gerrit_plugin(\n     ],\n     resources \u003d glob([\"src/main/resources/**/*\"]),\n     deps \u003d [\n-        \":ai-review-agent-provider-neverlink\",\n+        \":ai-review-agent-provider-api-neverlink\",\n         \"//lib/errorprone:annotations\",\n         \"@google-api-common//jar\",\n         \"@google-gemini//jar\",\n@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@ gerrit_plugin(\n )\n \n java_library(\n-    name \u003d \"ai-review-agent-provider-neverlink\",\n+    name \u003d \"ai-review-agent-provider-api-neverlink\",\n     neverlink \u003d True,\n-    exports \u003d [\"//plugins/ai-review-agent-provider\"],\n+    exports \u003d [\"//plugins/ai-review-agent-provider:ai-review-agent-provider-api\"],\n )\n```\n\nThat seems like a cleaner dependency boundary to me: the provider plugin would expose the shared API, while the concrete agent plugins would only consume that API rather than the whole plugin.",
